# Rust
/target
# Clippy gets its own, because check, clippy and test are three compile modes
# and sharing one directory makes them evict each other's fingerprints — the
# cost is a full rebuild on every alternation, not a slower one.
/target-lint
# Same reason, for the same three modes: a per-package run and the editor's
# analyser each get their own. Listed because one of them was not, and 2895
# build artifacts reached a commit before `git status` was read carefully.
/target-pkg
/target-ra
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Data / runtime
/data
*.db
*.log

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

